Possession of indecent photograph of child 293A. (1) Whoever has in his possession an indecent or obscene photograph or pseudo-photograph of a child shall be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years, fine or both.
(2) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (1): it shall be a defence for him to prove that -
(a) he had legitimate reason for having the photograph or pseudo-photograph in his possession;
(b) he had not himself seen the photograph or pseudo-photograph and did not know, nor had any cause to suspect, it to be indecent or obscene; or
(c) the photograph or pseudo-photograph was sent to him without any prior request made by him or on his behalf and that he did not keep it for an unreasonable time.
